-1a. the difference.

In Wix, categories are broad, primary groupings used to structure your core content or products, while tags are granular, specific labels used for detailed filtering and cross-referencing.

Key Differences in Wix

• Purpose and Scope
	• Categories: Act as the main directory or section for your items (e.g., Footwear in a store, or Tech on a blog). They define what an item is fundamentally about.
	• Tags: Act as specific keywords or attributes (e.g., sale, summer, vegan, wireless) that let visitors filter and find related content across different categories.
• URLs and SEO
	• Categories: Have dedicated, indexable landing page URLs (such as ://sitename.com) that search engines can crawl to understand your site structure and boost SEO.
	• Tags: Open a separate tag feed page (such as www.sitename.com/blog/tags/tag-title) that lists matching posts, though they serve a more functional filtering role rather than acting as primary SEO landing pages.
• Assignment Limits
	• Blog Categories: A blog post can usually be assigned up to 10 categories.
	• Blog Tags: You can assign up to 30 tags per blog post (with up to 4,000 total tags per site).
• Navigation and Display
	• Categories: Usually featured prominently in your main site menus, shop drop-downs, or header sections.
	• Tags: Often displayed in a tag cloud, a filter sidebar, or at the bottom of a post/product page for quick-clicking.


